Here is the list of results:

- The probability that all layers are valid \ud835\udf00-nets is $\ud835\udf11\ud835\udc3f$.
- The event that the greedy search at each layer returns a point within the \ud835\udf0c\ud835\udefenearest neighbors of the query in the layer below occurs with probability $\ud835\udefeper$ layer, and thus $\ud835\udefe\ud835\udc3facross all layers.
- The total running time is achieved with probability at least $(\ud835\udf11\ud835\udefe)\ud835\udc3ffor$\ud835\udc3f=log\ud835\udc5b$.
- The overall space usage of a HENN graph is linear in $\ud835\udc5b$, under the assumption that each proximity graph requires a linear space to the size of its underlying dataset.
